When working on an explicitly identified Jira ticket, use the configured
ticket-tracker MCP tools to create/find its record and read current state.
Use explicit item IDs and current revision tokens. Save actual MR links and
testing notes; record material changes or QA findings as rework.

Check prerequisites at approval requests, QA handoffs/retests, merge readiness,
and Done. QA fixes stay under QA; do not request a move back to implementation.
A draft is not a posted message. Record external approvals, posts, board moves,
and merges only after explicit user confirmation or actual verified evidence.
Do not remove QA or bypass requirements to satisfy a blocked transition.

If a tracker operation fails, report it plainly; do not claim state was saved.
For unrelated work, do not create tracker items or repeatedly mention the tool.
At handoffs, briefly state the next required action or external wait.

The app's Settings > Copilot screen previews the complete, scoped instruction
block and preserves existing user-level instructions when installing it.
